[{:db/id "q-123395/selection/2352cf5945fa67cc078f17de6591ed236f0bb6b0bfc66ccb68d4a53ec9e4f5f2" :answer/id #uuid "af9e16cc-4685-5e18-929a-7ce0c35d5ce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{12+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +8{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123395/selection/6bb28182289d2f1daaa4673c8025b396d3dae2b5f76adc70184d111fe2432867" :answer/id #uuid "3bcdbc98-96e1-5685-84f9-bc9b29f798c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{12+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +10{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123395/selection/13105bfd3ad5d87cef7d2fc6b35e44f4679b4b9f3ad2d197db31bdfdcfe6a38b" :answer/id #uuid "79bb08bb-f69c-5741-a16c-27d557048b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +12{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123395/selection/ebfcf332fd6cf8f4874749a5d28638a290125a72b0ce4e122b692c7d8e2762f1" :answer/id #uuid "7df4c2dd-5178-52e6-90f8-996a702152e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +12{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123395/selection/204691defd51f62f51e6ad0083409f2e1aae2a0dd058f37c16bf47cadc6ea812" :answer/id #uuid "396a1fe8-4087-5710-803a-41cbd7542e81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{17+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123395/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27b74778-f0a4-59c0-a80e-76e8680377fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123395/selection/204691defd51f62f51e6ad0083409f2e1aae2a0dd058f37c16bf47cadc6ea812" :answer-field/choices ["q-123395/selection/2352cf5945fa67cc078f17de6591ed236f0bb6b0bfc66ccb68d4a53ec9e4f5f2" "q-123395/selection/6bb28182289d2f1daaa4673c8025b396d3dae2b5f76adc70184d111fe2432867" "q-123395/selection/13105bfd3ad5d87cef7d2fc6b35e44f4679b4b9f3ad2d197db31bdfdcfe6a38b" "q-123395/selection/ebfcf332fd6cf8f4874749a5d28638a290125a72b0ce4e122b692c7d8e2762f1" "q-123395/selection/204691defd51f62f51e6ad0083409f2e1aae2a0dd058f37c16bf47cadc6ea812"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123395" :question/id #uuid "32311913-41b5-527d-a4e3-f4ddd4d7ca69" :question/math-academy-id "q-123395" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079137/assets/7dc83cbf45ec3025ad33552ce889c7ecb2daf73b426bc2fd10ec932f3311c92a.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=4+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta \\,$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{7\\pi }{6},$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=4+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(4+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡4\\theta +16{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +1+15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{17+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123395/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123395"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-123439"] :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $-\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le \\pi /2$ ?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({sec}^{3}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(3{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{-\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sec}^{6}⁡\\theta +9{sec}^{6}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sec}^{6}⁡\\theta (1+9{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta })\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-123355"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079137/assets/8fbf4c3074641b18d12dc7372378550f4c37e0b9b81843c2e57629c891a59263.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-123458/selection/6036074d3f4f325411e05eb8bd961ca2b57e4dd5fbcb3cca4c221f37cd84df8a" :answer/id #uuid "c3df67af-f00d-5fc6-9872-2eb4ddeb40dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123458/selection/de09ec3b9e53fa585686d5cca81fd750edff8ee72e4376b75b1583e72755287a" :answer/id #uuid "fbac9f9e-59fe-5a54-abe5-b57d11f13b38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123458/selection/1df3623a82ad993faa050736f6f1aec50a2af4a5427533c1078ad12647a0e5b2" :answer/id #uuid "f44e8831-87f8-56d6-910e-03cd5259a5c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{3+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123458/selection/65494cbacf729c0fd4818bf37b98bdf4170be69ee1b00cbbdd79d388a1c06851" :answer/id #uuid "f7ae0be9-189a-5c73-8d98-28895b4bece0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123458/selection/7ce0233c98a168bff4d1dcbfd8dd5fe56a3487e705dd4becb87199257294181b" :answer/id #uuid "52a27230-a60a-54db-bbac-6e41c0e4c7e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123458/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "31e1f9d6-a5cb-58f3-aad3-22370c46516b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123458/selection/7ce0233c98a168bff4d1dcbfd8dd5fe56a3487e705dd4becb87199257294181b" :answer-field/choices ["q-123458/selection/6036074d3f4f325411e05eb8bd961ca2b57e4dd5fbcb3cca4c221f37cd84df8a" "q-123458/selection/de09ec3b9e53fa585686d5cca81fd750edff8ee72e4376b75b1583e72755287a" "q-123458/selection/1df3623a82ad993faa050736f6f1aec50a2af4a5427533c1078ad12647a0e5b2" "q-123458/selection/65494cbacf729c0fd4818bf37b98bdf4170be69ee1b00cbbdd79d388a1c06851" "q-123458/selection/7ce0233c98a168bff4d1dcbfd8dd5fe56a3487e705dd4becb87199257294181b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123458" :question/id #uuid "9debd71f-7b2d-5a32-ae10-ca946736e9d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123458" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi $ ?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta }{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta })^{2}+{(\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta }{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )+\\frac{4{cos}^{2}⁡4\\theta }{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )^{2}+4(1-{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta )}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )^{2}+4(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )[1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta +4-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ]}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123458/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123458"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123371/selection/7d78e6b73dcbc968d3ba9e4d911e844e04f316ef8c305066693409ffbc25ee27" :answer/id #uuid "619e87e2-2970-56e2-b1aa-3a82680a7304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123371/selection/800ee2325d0170c85480daec409b8a8bdf663a0211cbbf01912af5a9703ec8fa" :answer/id #uuid "6ef5bbb5-8c66-58dd-8eb6-0bdba0125abb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123371/selection/6109147d0ad01d4c9f4dd01d52a5e10a1097af457465647fe2c123b668b387a1" :answer/id #uuid "c908d551-d19e-56d6-a8af-e18c984de601" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123371/selection/26552270d09800606620397baf62c90086cdda6cbd11cafb30f17f16dcb0b196" :answer/id #uuid "fe3b5b6c-ce88-5fea-b9fa-11f6a66b7402" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123371/selection/477efdebb94e82874c22fce5b9b7137ffadbb14aa03d387ca808606ed53ff740" :answer/id #uuid "73b1c951-342a-5210-bcd9-210d0ee43f8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123371/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "31a7053f-d225-545b-8f73-5ac62722f887" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123371/selection/800ee2325d0170c85480daec409b8a8bdf663a0211cbbf01912af5a9703ec8fa" :answer-field/choices ["q-123371/selection/7d78e6b73dcbc968d3ba9e4d911e844e04f316ef8c305066693409ffbc25ee27" "q-123371/selection/800ee2325d0170c85480daec409b8a8bdf663a0211cbbf01912af5a9703ec8fa" "q-123371/selection/6109147d0ad01d4c9f4dd01d52a5e10a1097af457465647fe2c123b668b387a1" "q-123371/selection/26552270d09800606620397baf62c90086cdda6cbd11cafb30f17f16dcb0b196" "q-123371/selection/477efdebb94e82874c22fce5b9b7137ffadbb14aa03d387ca808606ed53ff740"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123371" :question/id #uuid "e3fa9d74-2d47-5c4c-8f7f-aa45ff42e739" :question/math-academy-id "q-123371" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079137/assets/5b6490495c297b49d394b0f7c494fb35b710c8c4520ab898783877abdd079013.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +16{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +16{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +16}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{20-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123371/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123371"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123454/selection/b4c1ea8854411c1063411a09457e900390c72f892ce3a6ab2a11e3d9bec8d53b" :answer/id #uuid "ba8e70ad-fc59-5d6f-beba-eaa56e10c1b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123454/selection/4499d8f19d109b1dcbb9aed0038cd5542b1326a2018a69856532b0d2aff9810e" :answer/id #uuid "b41705ac-8db7-570c-8537-ef941cac412f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123454/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "d1202c9f-f0a6-5c21-9242-edb1453df43c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123454/selection/65ff4ab87d60a398b1ade186e194cec76e6222c17686528c05d44b6268962af9" :answer/id #uuid "9c45541a-8df5-524f-8265-1e661d250df5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\text{ }\\,\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123454/selection/b1603fad5fcbf593fd0559f564c88436c56ed4537180f9b4b555d2497180efe5" :answer/id #uuid "ba1157e8-5e94-5b25-a3e6-fb3ad5f5d987" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\text{ }\\,\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123454/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d29d7ba-5b21-534a-8b87-3a7e20b0816a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123454/selection/b1603fad5fcbf593fd0559f564c88436c56ed4537180f9b4b555d2497180efe5" :answer-field/choices ["q-123454/selection/b4c1ea8854411c1063411a09457e900390c72f892ce3a6ab2a11e3d9bec8d53b" "q-123454/selection/4499d8f19d109b1dcbb9aed0038cd5542b1326a2018a69856532b0d2aff9810e" "q-123454/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-123454/selection/65ff4ab87d60a398b1ade186e194cec76e6222c17686528c05d44b6268962af9" "q-123454/selection/b1603fad5fcbf593fd0559f564c88436c56ed4537180f9b4b555d2497180efe5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123454" :question/id #uuid "6fb03672-f783-5453-94bf-11f27f84fe3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-123454" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta })^{2}+{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )^{2}+{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\text{ }\\,\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123454/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5777905c-e581-5454-bdbe-29878ad1237b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123454"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149815/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8" :answer/id #uuid "21eac51e-3769-57f9-b0a9-d9fbeb7dab16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149815/selection/338fd6744eb7ca9587a541b0bb0183ee8b61d9b20649c5de8a38a7eb04c075d9" :answer/id #uuid "c800af60-4ba1-5753-a4f9-2acde06caf0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149815/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" :answer/id #uuid "a4e947cc-ca97-5982-b285-aee0e7828b6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149815/selection/03864569254141960db19b242c7f1e850d6147657a3c76f443bd0fefd8fede2f" :answer/id #uuid "b634834b-dfae-5225-899a-cc134bfc8177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149815/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" :answer/id #uuid "984c6f1b-0d37-5c82-bac3-29e6de683b44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149815/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75da1f98-504f-5d6f-ad0c-50f57f91a7f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149815/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" :answer-field/choices ["q-149815/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8" "q-149815/selection/338fd6744eb7ca9587a541b0bb0183ee8b61d9b20649c5de8a38a7eb04c075d9" "q-149815/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" "q-149815/selection/03864569254141960db19b242c7f1e850d6147657a3c76f443bd0fefd8fede2f" "q-149815/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149815" :question/id #uuid "ffe36308-1b34-5312-945e-995cf626c070" :question/math-academy-id "q-149815" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079137/assets/624bb949d80c1da50cba951b00210a2a26aeb3c44d77d4c2eed69c8e3ba0f4d4.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149815/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5777905c-e581-5454-bdbe-29878ad1237b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149815"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-123623"] :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta (1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-149817/selection/b62c79fdd95bf94e83a28cb1154beb3fb3e436831ed70648c82c4fb6fdf1fad7" :answer/id #uuid "aa23bf93-262b-5f9c-97d4-2e467d3c6cf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149817/selection/f5b59c38aedd64d30d352f867e142b0015b5dbd5800fae155af29e52cdf70579" :answer/id #uuid "0c295d3e-e463-53b3-9ea5-27d9bcb01308" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149817/selection/92cb8a4c11074a3ed6f545d2232faea4705c0f6ddc4e344ed520416533ac3cb3" :answer/id #uuid "56acaa9f-75af-53d5-893b-25e264700a6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149817/selection/de02fe1ba525497eab4b308e55896a10dc20d3c81b2a530e23aad4cba57709dc" :answer/id #uuid "4393d583-ddb1-58e4-884f-edc98b690ee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149817/selection/3b2e7538e6db4bc10a950897389f444b31767ca3e1e8e57049e9d58ed42cd847" :answer/id #uuid "6392e08e-51c5-5310-aad9-a6a6156ec566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149817/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cde81bf6-bc18-56f2-adc9-94386879ff4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149817/selection/92cb8a4c11074a3ed6f545d2232faea4705c0f6ddc4e344ed520416533ac3cb3" :answer-field/choices ["q-149817/selection/b62c79fdd95bf94e83a28cb1154beb3fb3e436831ed70648c82c4fb6fdf1fad7" "q-149817/selection/f5b59c38aedd64d30d352f867e142b0015b5dbd5800fae155af29e52cdf70579" "q-149817/selection/92cb8a4c11074a3ed6f545d2232faea4705c0f6ddc4e344ed520416533ac3cb3" "q-149817/selection/de02fe1ba525497eab4b308e55896a10dc20d3c81b2a530e23aad4cba57709dc" "q-149817/selection/3b2e7538e6db4bc10a950897389f444b31767ca3e1e8e57049e9d58ed42cd847"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149817" :question/id #uuid "466f452f-c6f1-5600-b5e8-775a4618b1bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-149817" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079137/assets/b2ce73d5a44c834b5935596e85293eb92039b674746754317846488dbba8d930.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={e}^{\\theta /4}\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={e}^{\\theta /4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\frac{1}{4}\\,{e}^{\\theta /4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{({e}^{\\theta /4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{4}\\,{e}^{\\theta /4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{e}^{\\theta /2}+\\frac{1}{16}\\,{e}^{\\theta /2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{16}\\,{e}^{\\theta /2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{e}^{\\theta /4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}\\,{e}^{\\theta /4}\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149817/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5777905c-e581-5454-bdbe-29878ad1237b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149817"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123587/selection/bfebe468245f622037d6851fb124d88104d59cfddc097fb8f02c309a052ef46c" :answer/id #uuid "ef2f194a-94dc-5b5a-91c2-3304d97e7779" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{({\\pi }^{2}+4)}^{3/2}-4}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123587/selection/35c532914f14fa39ba459a144cf58e09b764421255a51149b439a966f4536b19" :answer/id #uuid "532ca5bf-239b-5d8b-b504-5b7d330429cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{(\\pi +4)}^{1/2}-8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123587/selection/26d479b3dfe68479f4adb88bf026c4b702162a09ac754c56afc83377f9166b8c" :answer/id #uuid "ef963f3f-8da9-56ec-a5af-08d9b60af391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{(\\pi +2)}^{1/2}-8}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123587/selection/ad1b6e473e15c26fc317d34404a93a7991002924c795ee843690cae695bbe62f" :answer/id #uuid "8ac3cd23-cd71-58ac-9725-41dd46fc0962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{(\\pi +2)}^{3/2}-8}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123587/selection/f43cb6c474d6921d668bd5b04dcdcedd856f71f81b5bf45c3ff4161733e00aa7" :answer/id #uuid "7fe75ea4-d9ae-5836-be51-a71a7b2f6155" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{({\\pi }^{2}+4)}^{3/2}-8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123587/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "70c4f7f5-f1bf-568b-8c5f-f5af7c6c9181" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123587/selection/f43cb6c474d6921d668bd5b04dcdcedd856f71f81b5bf45c3ff4161733e00aa7" :answer-field/choices ["q-123587/selection/bfebe468245f622037d6851fb124d88104d59cfddc097fb8f02c309a052ef46c" "q-123587/selection/35c532914f14fa39ba459a144cf58e09b764421255a51149b439a966f4536b19" "q-123587/selection/26d479b3dfe68479f4adb88bf026c4b702162a09ac754c56afc83377f9166b8c" "q-123587/selection/ad1b6e473e15c26fc317d34404a93a7991002924c795ee843690cae695bbe62f" "q-123587/selection/f43cb6c474d6921d668bd5b04dcdcedd856f71f81b5bf45c3ff4161733e00aa7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123587" :question/id #uuid "503f24c8-4567-59f4-9d53-4a5aac72c1dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-123587" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079137/assets/994b8cd2134d6d1e9a1e89559e462128c05fd5d3e7f4755c51931f3cf7f37268.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={\\theta }^{2}\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={\\theta }^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{({\\theta }^{2})}^{2}+{(2\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{4}+4{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}(4+{\\theta }^{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\theta \\sqrt{4+{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\theta \\sqrt{4+{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\frac{{(4+{\\theta }^{2})}^{3/2}}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{{({\\pi }^{2}+4)}^{3/2}-8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123587/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5777905c-e581-5454-bdbe-29878ad1237b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123587"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9492"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079137/assets/cd1ba2536264e122c84377a1892c3ca86dd8f273b2eab9ba0e2c53eeb504ef65.png)\n\n  \n\nFind a definite integral with respect to $\\theta$ that's equivalent to $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\,\\textrm d s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=1-\\sin{\\theta}\\,$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq  \\pi,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\textrm d s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm ds = \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r = r(\\theta)$ for $\\theta_1 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\theta_2,$ we have\n\n$$\nL=\t\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=1-\\sin{\\theta},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = -\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9493"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079137/assets/a55339eae9b193813ab696538c85696ad5f4267e2e31513bdb2c8998cd711311.png)\n\n  \n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\,\\textrm d s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2(1+\\sin\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq {\\pi},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\textrm d s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm ds = \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r = r(\\theta)$ for $\\theta_1 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\theta_2,$ we have\n\n$$\nL=\t\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=2(1+\\sin\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = 2\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+4{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identities:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})=1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting our integral using the above identities, we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2}))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}((0+1)-(-1+0)) \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
